@startuml Checkout_Idempotency
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10

actor Client
participant "OrderController" as Controller
participant "IdempotencyService" as Idempotency
participant "CheckoutService" as Checkout
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Scenario 1: Duplicate Request (Same Idempotency Key) ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/orders/checkout\n{cartId, idempotencyKey="abc123"}
activate Controller

Controller -> Idempotency: getExistingResponse("abc123", userId, path)
activate Idempotency

Idempotency -> Idempotency: hashKey("abc123")
note right of Idempotency: SHA-256 hash

Idempotency -> DB: SELECT idempotency_keys\nWHERE key_hash = ?
DB --> Idempotency: IdempotencyKey (found, not expired)

Idempotency -> Idempotency: validateUserAndPath()
Idempotency -> Idempotency: checkExpired()

Idempotency --> Controller: IdempotencyResponse\n(statusCode=201, responseBody=JSON)
deactivate Idempotency

Controller -> Controller: deserializeResponse(responseBody)
Controller --> Client: 201 Created\nApiResponse<OrderResponse>\n(cached response)

note right of Controller: CheckoutService NOT called\nNo database writes\nIdempotent response returned

deactivate Controller

== Scenario 2: First Request (New Idempotency Key) ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/orders/checkout\n{cartId, idempotencyKey="xyz789"}
activate Controller

Controller -> Idempotency: getExistingResponse("xyz789", userId, path)
activate Idempotency

Idempotency -> Idempotency: hashKey("xyz789")
Idempotency -> DB: SELECT idempotency_keys\nWHERE key_hash = ?
DB --> Idempotency: Optional.empty()

Idempotency --> Controller: Optional.empty()
deactivate Idempotency

Controller -> Checkout: checkout(userId, cartId)
activate Checkout

... Checkout process (success) ...

Checkout --> Controller: Order
deactivate Checkout

Controller -> Controller: toOrderResponse(order)

Controller -> Idempotency: storeResponse("xyz789", userId, path, 201, response)
activate Idempotency

Idempotency -> Idempotency: hashKey("xyz789")
Idempotency -> Idempotency: serializeResponse(response)
Idempotency -> DB: INSERT INTO idempotency_keys\n(id, key_hash, user_id, request_path,\nresponse_status_code, response_body, expires_at, ...)
DB --> Idempotency: IdempotencyKey
Idempotency --> Controller: void
deactivate Idempotency

Controller --> Client: 201 Created\nApiResponse<OrderResponse>
deactivate Controller

== Scenario 3: Expired Idempotency Key ==

Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/orders/checkout\n{cartId, idempotencyKey="expired123"}
activate Controller

Controller -> Idempotency: getExistingResponse("expired123", userId, path)
activate Idempotency

Idempotency -> Idempotency: hashKey("expired123")
Idempotency -> DB: SELECT idempotency_keys\nWHERE key_hash = ?
DB --> Idempotency: IdempotencyKey (found, but expired)

Idempotency -> Idempotency: checkExpired()
Idempotency -> Idempotency: key.isExpired() == true

Idempotency --> Controller: Optional.empty()
deactivate Idempotency

note right of Controller: Expired key ignored\nProcess as new request

Controller -> Checkout: checkout(userId, cartId)
activate Checkout

... Checkout process (success) ...

Checkout --> Controller: Order
deactivate Checkout

Controller -> Idempotency: storeResponse("expired123", userId, path, 201, response)
Idempotency -> DB: INSERT INTO idempotency_keys\n(new record with new expires_at)
Idempotency --> Controller: void

Controller --> Client: 201 Created\nApiResponse<OrderResponse>
deactivate Controller

@enduml
